   "flag": "Missing option / outdated premise: the current RDS User Guide says RDS for SQL Server joins a self-managed AD domain directly wherever it is hosted ('eliminating the need for complex intermediary domains or forest trusts'), and the stem says the on-premises domain controllers are reachable from the VPC, so the least-overhead solution (join the DB instance directly to the on-premises domain) is not offered; B (EC2 domain controllers of the same domain) then also works with RDS self-managed AD, so the key A rests only on 'managed is less overhead than EC2 DCs', and any explanation that says RDS needs AWS Managed Microsoft AD (fact directory-service-rds-needs-managed-ad) is no longer true for SQL Server.",
